/-
# Involutions centralized by an involutory automorphism (Kourovka Notebook Problem 7.15)

Kourovka Notebook, Problem 7.15 (R. Griess), marked solved in the 21st issue: prove that if `F*(G)`
is quasisimple and `α ∈ Aut G`, `|α| = 2`, then `C_G(α)` contains an involution outside `Z(F*(G))`,
except when `F*(G)` has quaternion Sylow `2`-subgroups.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.IsSubnormal
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Nilpotent
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Quaternion
public import Mathlib.Order.CompletePartialOrder
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentThreeConjugatesFittingKourovka17Problem40Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.QuasisimpleInvolutionCentralizerKourovka7Problem15Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 7.15 (R. Griess). UnsolvedMath record
UM-00700416 (`KOU-7.15`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`G` is finite. The definitions follow the resolving preprint: `G` is quasisimple when it is perfect
and `G / Z(G)` is non-abelian simple; `F(G)` is the Fitting subgroup (`fittingSubgroup` of the
Kourovka 17.40 entry, reused here: generated by the normal nilpotent subgroups), `E(G)` the layer
(generated by the subnormal quasisimple subgroups, the components) and `F*(G) = F(G) E(G)`; `C_G(α)`
is the fixed-point set of `α`; an involution is an element of order `2`. "Quaternion" is read as
generalized quaternion of order at least `8` (`IsGeneralizedQuaternion` of `GroupClassesShared`:
`QuaternionGroup (2 ^ k)`, `k ≥ 1`), the reading of the preprint; this is the larger exception, so
the refuted statement is the weaker claim. The Sylow subgroups of `F*(G)` are conjugate, so
excluding generalized quaternion ones for all of them is the same as for one.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared (IsGeneralizedQuaternion)
open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentThreeConjugatesFittingKourovka17Problem40Wanted
  (fittingSubgroup)

/-- `G` is quasisimple: `G` is perfect and `G / Z(G)` is simple (hence non-abelian simple). -/
def IsQuasisimple (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  commutator G = ⊤ ∧ IsSimpleGroup (G ⧸ Subgroup.center G)

/-- The layer `E(G)`: the subgroup generated by the components of `G`, its subnormal quasisimple
subgroups. -/
def layer (G : Type*) [Group G] : Subgroup G :=
  ⨆ (K : Subgroup G) (_ : K.IsSubnormal ∧ IsQuasisimple K), K

/-- The generalized Fitting subgroup `F*(G) = F(G) E(G)`. -/
def generalizedFittingSubgroup (G : Type*) [Group G] : Subgroup G :=
  fittingSubgroup G ⊔ layer G

/-- Kourovka 7.15 (R. Griess): if `G` is finite, `F*(G)` is quasisimple without generalized
quaternion Sylow `2`-subgroups, and `α` is an automorphism of `G` of order `2`, then `C_G(α)`
contains an involution outside `Z(F*(G))`. -/
def quasisimpleInvolutoryCentralizer : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsQuasisimple (generalizedFittingSubgroup G) →
    (∀ P : Sylow 2 (generalizedFittingSubgroup G), ¬ IsGeneralizedQuaternion P) →
    ∀ α : MulAut G, orderOf α = 2 →
      ∃ g : G, α g = g ∧ orderOf g = 2 ∧
        g ∉ (Subgroup.center (generalizedFittingSubgroup G)).map
          (generalizedFittingSubgroup G).subtype

/--
Resolved false: the 21st issue marks 7.15 solved, "This is not always true", citing Jayadevan's 2026
preprint (an AI-generated solution confirmed by A. Rizzoli). Its Theorem 1.1 gives a finite perfect
group `E` with `Z(E) = ⟨z⟩` of order `2` and `E / Z(E) ≅ A₈` and an automorphism `α` of order `2`
whose fixed elements of square `1` are exactly `1` and `z`; `E` contains `C₂ × C₂`, so its Sylow
`2`-subgroups are not generalized quaternion, and `F*(E) = E` because `E` is quasisimple. Source: E.
I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 7.15 (R. Griess); resolution: A. Jayadevan, An involutory
automorphism of a double cover of A8 with central fixed involutions, preprint, Zenodo, 2026
(AI-generated solution confirmed by A. Rizzoli), Kourovka Notebook 21st issue, Problem 7.15, marked
solved: This is not always true; preprint, Theorem 1.1, https://zenodo.org/records/22750993.
-/
public theorem_wanted quasisimpleInvolutoryCentralizer_refuted : ¬ quasisimpleInvolutoryCentralizer

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.QuasisimpleInvolutionCentralizerKourovka7Problem15Wanted
